// Main, changed so both threads share ONE account
BankAccount shared = new BankAccount(1000);

Thread t1 = new Thread(new WithdrawTask(shared, 700), "T1");
Thread t2 = new Thread(new WithdrawTask(shared, 700), "T2");

t1.start();
t2.start();
t1.join();
t2.join();

System.out.println(shared.getBalance());

Now both threads share one account of 1000 and each asks for 700, WITH the synchronized block in place. What is printed, and how many withdrawals succeed?,"-400, because both withdrawals go through","300, and only ONE withdrawal succeeds. The second thread waits, then sees that 700 is more than the remaining 300 and returns without doing anything","300, and both withdrawals succeed","1000, because both are rejected",,2,"Verified: 300 on all 8 runs. The lock does not make both withdrawals work - it makes the second one correctly fail, which is the whole point.",2

